1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:14,241
Every part gets a label. On the Nesting tab, Labels shows where each one goes on the sheet.

2
00:00:14,241 --> 00:00:17,578
Label spots are picked per part: the largest clear area, away from holes and edges.

3
00:00:17,578 --> 00:00:21,471
The label files are made on the Output tab.

4
00:00:21,471 --> 00:00:26,906
Labels PDF: one 100 x 70 mm label per part, with a sheet header label first.

5
00:00:26,906 --> 00:00:35,521
Each label: part ID barcode, cabinet and part name, size, edge diagram, sheet and cut order.

6
00:00:35,521 --> 00:00:41,221
Sheet maps PDF: one page per sheet showing every part, its label spot and the machine origin.

7
00:00:41,221 --> 00:00:46,532
Stick the labels where the map shows, and every part is identified as it comes off the table.

8
00:00:46,532 --> 00:00:49,957
Labels ZPL sends the same labels straight to a Zebra label printer.
